# ModelUnify versioning

- Use `scripts/_version.py` (`MODELUNIFY_VERSION`) as the canonical version.
- For each delivered change set, bump the version and add a dated `CHANGELOG.md` entry describing changes, validation and material limitations.
- Increment the current patch version for fixes, the minor version for features, and the major version for breaking changes. Follow an explicitly requested version instead when provided.
- Keep the canonical value numeric (for example `1.9`); the interface may display `v1.9`.
- Preserve historical release entries and existing distribution labels. Only label a distribution with the version of the source actually built into it.
- Versioning does not authorize Git commits, publishing, dependency installation or rebuilding distributions.
